      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RAVENITE (8) has attracted solid market support at his past two starts without delivering, but he is probably better over this shorter trip. The wins have been hard to come by, but from a good gate in this, he should be right in the finish. Follow your money. UNIFIES (1) resumes after 5 months away and he has won a tune-up trial at Rockhampton very easily just over a week ago. He has enough ability to make an immediate impact. BILLY BOOM (3) showed plenty of determination when scoring at Rockhampton two runs ago and is more than capable of bouncing back after his latest effort for seventh which was over a trip that was a tad too long for him. Stick with him in this. EXCELBOOM (6) has been racing consistently, highlighted by a strong second at a recent Oak Park picnic meeting, and he should be competitive again. MOOCHI STARLIGHT (5) has enjoyed an excellent campaign with two victories and a narrow runner-up finish last time out, making her another genuine winning chance.",
